l."}],"$undefined"]}]]}]}],["$","section","Squid makes its generation contract explicit",{"id":"squid-makes-its-generation-contract-explicit","className":"scroll-mt-28 py-12 sm:py-14","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-[4rem_minmax(0,1fr)] md:gap-8","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-sm text-primary","children":"03"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-balance text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.025em] sm:text-3xl","children":"Squid makes its generation contract explicit"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-[1.05rem] leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"The main Squid path requires a complete multi-file React + TypeScript app, checks internal import resolution and export style, and refuses incomplete output. The UI then exposes a quality report and the export pipeline adds another verification layer around the runnable bundle."}],"$undefined"]}]]}]}],["$","section","Git integration and a verified ZIP serve different teams",{"id":"git-integration-and-a-verified-zip-serve-different-teams","className":"scroll-mt-28 py-12 sm:py-14","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-[4rem_minmax(0,1fr)] md:gap-8","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-mono text-sm text-primary","children":"04"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-balance text-2xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.025em] sm:text-3xl","children":"Git integration and a verified ZIP serve different teams"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 text-[1.05rem] leading-8 text-muted-foreground","children":"v0's bidirectional Git workflow is attractive when a repository is already the center of collaboration. Squid's self-describing ZIP is useful when a founder or designer wants a clear handoff artifact without configuring Git first. A mature engineering team may reasonably prefer Git; a fast transfer may benefit from the packaged export."}],"$undefined"]}]]}]}],"$L4e"]}]
